  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "zombie_as_metaphor",
  "label": "The use of zombies as a metaphor for marginalized or dehumanized groups",
  "description": "Zombies are often used as a metaphor for marginalized or dehumanized groups in popular culture, often to depict their perceived lack of humanity or agency. In the meme, zombies are used as a metaphor for people of color, implying that because they are not racially defined, they are not human and therefore their killing cannot be classified as homicide. This requires understanding of the use of zombies as a metaphor in popular culture and its implications.",
